# REGRESSION PIN — indirect-call `&`-param ABI, TYPE axis cell: **enum /
# `Option[int]`** (a non-resource aggregate that is NOT a user struct), through
# an ANNOTATED LOCAL `Callable`. This cell is the one the C backend's own
# comment names as "by-value non-resource aggregate", and it was broken at base
# exactly like the struct cells — enum payloads are not a separate class.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the PRE-fix compiler (`git checkout -- src && cargo build`):
#     C    -> rc 139 (SIGSEGV)
#     LLVM -> rc 139 (SIGSEGV)
# POST-fix both backends print `7`.
#
# LANE AXIS (self-host driver): rc 139 — same class, filed separately.
#
# WHY known_gaps/: zero parity-corpus inflow; the LIVE test asserts on C + LLVM.
#
# INTENDED: `7` (the callee replaces the whole `Option` through the `&`).
void bump(Option[int] &o):
    o = Some(7)

int main():
    Callable[void(Option[int] &)] f = bump
    Option[int] o = Some(1)
    f(&o)
    match o:
        case Some(v):
            print(v)
        else:
            print(-1)
    return 0
